],"supported_intervals":["1m","5m","15m","30m","1h","4h","1d","1w","1mo"],"supported_plots":["fast","slow"]},{"filter_type":"FILTER_TYPE_SUPPORT","display_name":"Support","filter_group":"TECHNICAL","value_type":"DECIMAL","unit_type":"PLAIN","supported_predicates":[">",">=","<","<="],"supported_intervals":["1d","1w","1m"],"supported_plots":["support1","support2"]},{"filter_type":"FILTER_TYPE_VWAP","display_name":"VWAP","filter_group":"TECHNICAL","value_type":"DECIMAL","unit_type":"PLAIN","supported_predicates":[">",">=","<","<=","BETWEEN","OUTSIDE"],"supported_intervals":["1m","5m","15m","30m","1h","4h","1d","1w","1mo"]},{"filter_type":"FILTER_TYPE_WILLIAMS_PERCENT_RANGE","display_name":"Williams Percent Range","filter_group":"TECHNICAL","value_type":"DECIMAL","unit_type":"PLAIN","supported_predicates":[">",">=","<","<=","BETWEEN","OUTSIDE"],"supported_lengths":[10,14,20,25],"supported_intervals":["1m","5m","15m","30m","1h","4h","1d","1w","1mo"]}]},"guide":"Match filter_type exactly, including suffixes (e.g. percent-change filters use FILTER_TYPE_PERCENT_CHANGE_FROM_CLOSE, not FILTER_TYPE_PERCENT_CHANGE). If a filter's supported_intervals is non-empty, pass an interval -- omitting it is the leading cause of an otherwise-valid filter returning no results. Use supported_predicates symbols exactly (e.g. \">\", \"BETWEEN\"). No enum filter scopes a scan to particular instruments: to restrict it to named tickers or to an index's members, use an expression filter on the symbol field (get_scanner_datapoints, descriptive category) rather than concluding it cannot be done. If a filter has options, its values must come from that list verbatim -- it is the filter's complete vocabulary, and anything else is rejected. Do not infer these values from scan results: the instrument_type field in results is Robinhood's classification, which is coarser than the asset-type filter's (its EQUITY spans both STOCK and ETF), so a value copied from there screens for nothing. Filters with unit_type PERCENTAGE take DECIMAL values: 0.05 means 5%. A whole-percent number silently matches nothing -- \"implied volatility above 80\" is values [\"0.8\"], because [\"80\"] reads as 8000% and returns zero rows with no error. This applies to every PERCENTAGE filter (implied and historical volatility, IV rank, the margins, return on assets/equity, % change, gap)."}
